# Copy to .pii-denylist (gitignored) and add your own terms.
#
# The list is itself sensitive — it is your name, handle, employer and account
# nicknames — so the real one never enters the repository. CI reads it from a
# repository secret. One term per line; matching is case-insensitive.
#
# Its absence weakens the scan but never blocks it, so a fresh clone still runs.

# Your legal name and any variants you sign with
# Your GitHub handle
# Your employer
# Any account nickname you use in conversation
# Your personal and work email domains
